From: spycat88 <spycat88@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: Add Eliza MDSS compatible

Add the Eliza (SM7750) MDSS compatible to the clients list, so it gets an
identity domain at boot, as SM8550, SM8650 and SM8750 do with the
previous patches.

The bootloader leaves its picture scanning out at kernel entry. Without
an identity domain the MDSS stream is attached to an empty translating
domain as soon as the device is added, and its fetches fault until the
DPU driver stops the timing engine and attaches its own domain. On the
Retroid Pocket Duo every boot logged, right after the Wi-Fi device was
added to its iommu group, as many of these as the rate limit lets
through:

  arm-smmu 15000000.iommu: Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x402,
  iova=0xfc813700, fsynr=0x690021, cbfrsynra=0x800, cb=8
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -408,6 +408,7 @@
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,adreno" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,adreno-gmu" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,eliza-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdp4" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdss" },
